== Effects ==
* On use, Isaac raises the candle above his head. On pressing a fire button, a red flame, similar to a {{E|Red Fire Place}}, will fire in the chosen direction. It can pass over pits, but can not travel through [[obstacles]].
** {{dlc|nr}} The flame deals 23 damage per tick, and can hit up to 5 times for a maximum of 115 damage per flame.
** {{dlc|r}} The flame can hit up to 4 times, and the damage decreases as the flame shrinks. The first hit deals 23 damage, the second hit deals 17.5 damage, and the last two ticks deal 11.5 damage, for a maximum of 63.25 damage per flame.
** The flame also destroys enemy shots it comes into contact with, which decreases its size each time being hit until the flame is entirely extinguished by this process.
** {{dlc|nr}} The flame projectile is persistent and will remain active in the [[room]] until it deals a set amount of damage.
** {{dlc|r}} Flames will disappear automatically after 10 seconds.

== Notes ==
* {{dlc|nr}} While Isaac holds the candle above his head, his movement speed is reduced.
* {{Dlc|nr}} There is no limit to the number of fires that can be active. This is useful in situations where mob spawning can be controlled: for example, beating {{R|Boss Rush}} or [[Greed Mode]] as {{C|The Lost}}. This is time-consuming but can be viable if other sources of damage are weak or unreliable.
* {{Dlc|nr}} It will block Isaac's tears but won't burn him. Isaac's tears can also shrink the size of the flame.
* {{dlc|r}} Flames do not block Isaac's shots, nor are they put out by them.
* Flames will destroy {{e|Shopkeeper}}s.
* {{dlc|r}} Flames will turn certain enemies (such as {{E|Hopper}}s and {{E|Clotty|text=Clotties}}) into their flaming variants, making them stronger. The flame is unable to damage these monsters.

== Synergies ==
* {{Book of Virtues synergy|description=Spawns red wisps in the middle ring. The wisps shoot small flames instead of tears, with a very high tear delay; flames last for 5 seconds or until they block 2 shots and/or deal 2 ticks of damage. The wisps do not persist between rooms, and the damage they deal does not increase with {{I|BFFS!}} or scale up on later floors.}}

